# What sits at the package root and is not package content. The archive is
# the manifest's closure, so none of this would ship anyway; naming it here
# is what says the omission was decided rather than forgotten.

# Build output. The four .wasm files the lib SQL names are pulled back in by
# the closure; the rest of the directory stays out. build/ is the X-CLIP
# ONNX export, an input to that build.
target/
build/

# The wit each module's build.rs copies out of the installed ffrwd/wasm.
wit/

# The Rust workspace that builds the four modules. The modules ship; their
# sources are read on GitHub.
Cargo.toml
Cargo.lock
clips/
sounds/
embed/
embed_clip/

# The check script the manifest's "test" runs and the X-CLIP export script,
# both of which run in a checkout and neither of which an installed package
# reaches for.
scripts/

# Local development state: which archive of each dependency this checkout
# resolved to, which a consumer solves for itself.
ffrwd.lock
